-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/6e2e0e44-f9e4-4cc3-b68e-107f3b0f4477
-- title:
--   The final capped restart stage is dominated by iterated capped returns
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, $I=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, $E=I\times\{0,1\}$, and $\Omega=\mathcal P(E)$. Let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean oracles on subsets of $I$. Write $R(S)$ for the natural-number value of the paired-rank routine with parameter $r$ and these oracles, and $d(S)=n-R(S)$ with subtraction truncated at zero. Let $M_1,M_2$ be matroids with ground set $I$ and common rank $r$, and assume $o_j$ returns true exactly on independent sets of $M_j$, for $j=1,2$. Let $p=(\varepsilon,\delta)$ consist of rational parameters $0<\varepsilon,\delta<1$. Write $s=\operatorname{setup}(n,p)$ for the prescribed annealing schedule, $L=s.L$ for its phase count, $\rho=s.\rho$ for its temperature ratio, $\eta=s.\eta$ for its relative mean tolerance, and $N=s.\mathrm{observations}$ for its sample count. A transversal selects one label from each pair; let $T$ be this class. For distinct $i,k\in I$, let $D_{ik}$ be the class having pair $i$ empty, pair $k$ full, and every other pair singly occupied. All other states are invalid. For $q>0$ and positive rational multipliers $w_{ik}$, define $C(q)=\sum_{S\in T}q^{d(S)}$, $D_{ik}(q)=\sum_{S\in D_{ik}}q^{d(S)}$, and $\lambda(S)=q^{d(S)}$ on $T$, $\lambda(S)=w_{ik}q^{d(S)}$ on $D_{ik}$, and $\lambda(S)=0$ on invalid states. Let $Z_w=\sum_S\lambda(S)$ and $\pi(S)=\lambda(S)/Z_w$. The observable indices form $\mathcal O=\{0,1\}\sqcup(I\times I)$. Their functions are $G_0=\mathbf1_T$, $G_1=\mathbf1_T\rho^{d(S)}$, and $G_{ik}=\mathbf1_{D_{ik}}$ for $i\ne k$, with $G_{ii}=\mathbf1_T$. At phase $j$, their true means are taken under the normalized operational law at $q=\rho^j$ and the current multipliers. Empirical means are the corresponding observation-counter averages. A phase cursor $u$ contains a current multiplier table, stored tables, a running product, and a bit cursor. Call it good at phase $j$ if every stored table at level $a\le j$ lies between one quarter and four times $C(\rho^a)/D_{ik}(\rho^a)$, and its current table has the same bounds at level $j$, for all distinct $i,k$. Say phase $j$ has accurate raw means if its actual phase history reaches a good cursor, its restart and observation procedures succeed, $N>0$, and every empirical observable mean lies between $(1-\eta)$ and $(1+\eta)$ times its true mean. Call an observation completed when those operational procedures succeed from a good reached cursor and $N>0$, without requiring mean accuracy. Define $e_\ell(\beta)$ to be the squared empirical-minus-true error for observable $\ell$ on completed observations and zero otherwise. A certified phase is a successful actual phase step from a good cursor whose product is multiplied by a ratio $R_j$ satisfying $(1-\eta)/(1+\eta)\le R_j/(C(\rho^{j+1})/C(\rho^j))\le(1+\eta)/(1-\eta)$, and whose next cursor is good whenever another phase remains. Let $m=\operatorname{blockLength}(n,r,p)$ be the prescribed finite run-tape length. A Boolean list $\beta$ is read as a tape with value false beyond its end. Let $Y(\beta)$ be the rational result of the capped single annealing run on that tape with schedule $s$. Uniform $m$-bit tapes assign mass $2^{-m}$ to each list of length $m$. A successful prefix $h$ at phase $j$ is the consumed prefix of some length-$m$ tape whose phases before $j$ are certified; its length is the reached phase cursor, or zero if no cursor is reached. For such a fixed prefix put $t=m-|h|$, using truncated subtraction, and average over all $t$-bit suffixes $v$ appended to $h$. Assume $n>0$, positive common-base count, and $j<L$. Let $u$ be a fixed good cursor at phase $j$ with positive current multipliers, and assume that every suffix $v\in\{0,1\}^t$ makes the actual phase history on $hv$ reach exactly $u$. Use $\pi,P$ for the operational law and ideal Metropolis kernel at $q=\rho^j$ and the current table of $u$. Assume also $j>0$ and positivity of the stored table $u.\mathrm{tables}(j)$. Let $P_j$ be the ideal exchange kernel at $\rho^j$ using that stored table, $b=s.\mathrm{restartCap}$, and $\tau=s.\tau$. Let $K_b(x,y)$ be the probability of a positive-time first return to $T$ at $y$ within $b$ steps of $P_j$, starting at $x$. For $a\in\mathbb N$, define $R_a(S)$ as the uniform suffix mass of success at state $S$ of the actual restart with $a$ stages, begun at the bit cursor of $u$ with its stored tables. Then $$R_j(S)\le\sum_{x\in\Omega}R_{j-1}(x)K_b^\tau(x,S)\qquad(S\in\Omega).$$
